      - Branch-protection rulesets (only-develop→main / feature→develop Actions) — ready, blocked on GitHub Teams
      - The features-flow / multitenancy roadmap; co-owns the DMG deployment with Nick
      - 🔴 Discovered + is investigating the cross-fork DATA-LEAK with GitHub support (E17)
      - Onboards/coaches (showed Sam how to open a PR)
    totem_affinity: [ROOT, DEVOPS, QA]

  sam:
    display: Sam  (GitHub: samdeskin)
    title: "Co-founder — Product / Business (self-declared NON-developer)"   # confirmed: "I am not a developer"
    org: app-agent
    footprint:
      - Builds OpenJurist (his legal site; Drupal 6 → App Agent, ~80+ hrs) as the flagship field-test; Justia data partner
      - THE agent-behavior spec (80-hr feedback: verify-watchdog, clickable URLs, one-question intake, dev dashboard, no-secrets-in-context, per-task model choice)
      - Authored the framework-standards trio: AGENT_WORKING_STANDARD (work) · RELEASE_PROTOCOL (ship) · AI_OPERATIONS_CHARTER (operate); + SECURITY_HANDOFF, STATUS.md/docs-lint pattern
      - Drafts the business-model + equity contract + pricing-proposal.html (4-tier ladder + partner channel)
      - Self-healing / Hermes-agent vision; heavy Fable-5 evangelist ("Fable is a game changer, Opus sucks compared to Fable")
    totem_affinity: [FOUNDERS, ARCHITECT, QA]
    note: earlier v1 mislabeled Sam a "framework engineer" — CORRECTED. He drives via AI (Opus/Fable), not by hand.

